SecurityConfiguration.java adapts the API-key configuration pattern in
samples/sample-mcp-server-api-key/.../McpServerConfiguration.java.
Changes: environment-provided secrets, three trusted identity IDs, startup
validation, stateless authenticated MCP endpoint, deny-all other paths,
strict credential-header format, sanitized tool preflight.

API-key parsing, BCrypt authentication and the in-memory credential repository
are provided by the upstream dependency, not original P3 implementations.
MCP protocol and HTTP transport are provided by Spring AI / the MCP Java SDK.
See docs/upstream-vs-custom.md for the full boundary of original project work.

Python integration addition (2026-10-23):
The official modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk provides MCP client protocol and
Streamable HTTP; LangGraph provides StateGraph execution; LangChain and
langchain-openai provide message/tool-calling/model adapters. Their own licenses
apply to those dependencies; no dependency source or model weights are vendored.
The new bounded Agent, contracts, controlled credential/grant binding, error
conversion and cross-language fixtures/tests are P3 project additions, with AI
assistance. Existing Java authentication attribution and Apache-2.0 notices are
unchanged. See python-agent/README.md and docs/python-agent-verification.md.
